---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import FinalCTA from '../components/FinalCTA.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About DataDecision and founder Ashish Jha"
  description="DataDecision is a founder-led, measurement-first consultancy. Meet founder Ashish Jha and read the principles behind its AI-search visibility work."
  path="/about/"
  schema={[
    {
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'AboutPage',
      name: 'About DataDecision',
      url: 'https://datadecision.consulting/about/',
      mainEntity: {
        '@type': 'Organization',
        name: 'DataDecision',
        email: 'contact@datadecision.consulting',
        founder: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Ashish Jha' },
      },
    },
    {
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'Person',
      name: 'Ashish Jha',
      jobTitle: 'Founder',
      url: 'https://datadecision.consulting/about/',
      email: 'contact@datadecision.consulting',
      alumniOf: { '@type': 'CollegeOrUniversity', name: 'NIT Surat' },
      worksFor: {
        '@type': 'Organization',
        name: 'DataDecision',
        url: 'https://datadecision.consulting/',
      },
    },
  ]}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />
  <header class="shell page-hero page-hero--compact">
    <div class="page-hero__copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">About DataDecision</p><h1>
        A focused practice for better growth decisions.
      </h1><p class="lede">
        A focused consultancy for B2B SaaS teams that need a defensible view of AI-search visibility
        and the measurement path into pipeline.
      </p>
    </div><aside class="page-hero__aside">
      <div class="folio"><span>Company description</span><span>01 line</span></div><p
        class="lede"
        style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.8rem;"
      >
        Focused on AI-search visibility, measurement foundations and scoped implementation.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </header>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="founder-heading">
    <div class="shell founder-record">
      <div class="founder-record__identity">
        <p class="eyebrow">Founder</p>
        <h2 id="founder-heading">Ashish Jha</h2>
        <p class="small">Founder, DataDecision<br />Graduate, NIT Surat</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="mailto:contact@datadecision.consulting">
          contact@datadecision.consulting
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="founder-record__body">
        <p class="lede">
          Ashish Jha founded DataDecision to build a measurement-first practice for AI-search
          visibility and the path into pipeline.
        </p>
        <p class="measure">
          Ashish defines the observation frame before interpreting the output, keeps the important
          limits visible and recommends work the evidence can support. That discipline shapes every
          DataDecision engagement.
        </p>
        <dl class="founder-record__facts">
          <div>
            <dt>Education</dt>
            <dd>NIT Surat</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Education note</dt>
            <dd class="small">This identifies Ashish’s education and implies no endorsement.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid editorial-grid--reverse">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why this exists</p><h2>Evidence should survive the handoff.</h2>
      </div><div>
        <p class="lede">
          A useful growth number should carry enough context to make a decision. That matters as
          discovery spreads across search pages, generated answers, review sources and conversations
          that no single dashboard can fully observe.
        </p><p class="measure">
          DataDecision concentrates on the measurement layer: establish what is visible, identify
          what the existing stack misses and rank the work most likely to improve the next decision.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section--bright">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Operating principles</p><h2>How the work is judged.</h2>
      </div><div class="rule-list">
        <div class="rule-row">
          <span class="mono">01</span><div>
            <h3>Start with the observation</h3><p>
              Describe what happened, when it happened and how it was recorded.
            </p>
          </div><span class="rule-row__meta">Claim discipline</span>
        </div><div class="rule-row">
          <span class="mono">02</span><div>
            <h3>Record the baseline</h3><p>
              Establish the starting point before proposing a change.
            </p>
          </div><span class="rule-row__meta">Comparability</span>
        </div><div class="rule-row">
          <span class="mono">03</span><div>
            <h3>Publish the method</h3><p>
              Publish the rules needed to interrogate a number without disclosing private client
              data.
            </p>
          </div><span class="rule-row__meta">Transparency</span>
        </div><div class="rule-row">
          <span class="mono">04</span><div>
            <h3>Name uncertainty precisely</h3><p>
              Record unknown, unavailable and ambiguous observations as separate states.
            </p>
          </div><span class="rule-row__meta">Honesty</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section--ink">
    <div class="shell editorial-grid editorial-grid--balanced">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow" style="color:#9fd2bc;">Working relationship</p><h2>
          Clear access and clear handoffs.
        </h2>
      </div><div>
        <p class="lede" style="color:#d3d6d1;">
          You work directly with Ashish from the first fit review through the final Decision Board.
          Before work begins, you receive a written scope covering the question, inputs, timing, fee
          and expected deliverables.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FinalCTA heading="Start with a question the evidence can answer." />
</BaseLayout>
